<section class="section" id="technology">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header centered">
            <div class="section-label">Massage Intelligence</div>
            <h2 class="accent-heading">Panasonic Massage Technology — In Plain Language</h2>
            <p>Panasonic uses proprietary terminology for their chair technologies. Here's what each system actually does and how it translates into what you feel during a session.</p>
        </div>



<div style="margin-bottom:40px;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.10)">
  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0813/4036/7096/files/panasonic-tech-viz.jpg?v=1776368399" alt="Panasonic massage chair technology visualization — Real Pro Ultra mechanism, 1260P body scan, heated roller zones" style="width:100%;display:block;" loading="lazy">
</div>

<div class="tech-grid">
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">Real Pro Ultra H.I.</span>
                <h3>Human Intelligence Massage Mechanism</h3>
                <p>The core massage engine in Panasonic's flagship MAN1. "H.I." stands for Human Intelligence — a system that combines pressure sensors, microprocessor control, and multi-directional roller movement to replicate the responsiveness of a trained masseuse. Your massage adjusts in real time based on what the mechanism detects.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">1260P Acupoint Body Scan</span>
                <h3>Precision Body Mapping</h3>
                <p>Before your session begins, the chair scans and maps up to 1,260 acupressure points across your body. This creates a detailed profile of your spine curvature, shoulder position, and muscle contours — so rollers know exactly where to apply pressure and exactly where to avoid.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">SL-Track</span>
                <h3>Extended Roller Coverage Path</h3>
                <p>The SL-Track is Panasonic's roller rail path. Instead of stopping at the lower back (like many L-Track or S-Track systems), it extends from your neck down through the lower back and continues to the upper hamstring area. This means the rollers cover more of your back and glutes in a single pass.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">Junetsu Ultra Kneading</span>
                <h3>Micro-Circular Thumb Massage</h3>
                <p>Junetsu is a Panasonic-developed kneading technique that mimics the small, circular thumb motion a skilled massage therapist uses to break through deep tension knots. It creates a penetrating, focused massage that feels deliberate rather than mechanical.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">Infrared-Heated Rollers</span>
                <h3>Heat Where the Massage Happens</h3>
                <p>Unlike generic heated pads that warm a wide area, Panasonic integrates infrared heat directly into the massage rollers. The warmth is applied precisely where the rollers are working — loosening muscle tissue right at the point of contact for deeper, more effective results.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">Reflexology Foot Massage</span>
                <h3>Structured Sole + Arch Kneading</h3>
                <p>Air cells secure your feet while dedicated sole rollers perform shiatsu-style kneading along your arches and pressure points. Unlike basic foot vibration, this feels like intentional, placed pressure — the kind you'd experience from a reflexologist.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">Bodygrip Air Cells</span>
                <h3>Lower Body Compression System</h3>
                <p>Enlarged air cells wrap around your hips, thighs, and calves — applying rhythmic compression that stabilizes your lower body during the massage. This creates a "held" sensation that makes the session feel more complete and grounded.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-card">
                <span class="tech-card-name">In-Home Service Warranty</span>
                <h3>Ownership Without Worry</h3>
                <p>Panasonic's warranty coverage includes in-home service — trained technicians come to you. This separates Panasonic from brands that require you to ship parts or visit a repair center. For a high-ticket wellness purchase, this level of post-purchase confidence is a meaningful differentiator.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

